WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.850
It's the perfect time of year to hunker down
inside for a movie night or dedicate a weekend

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.300
to binge-watching a new series.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.960
There's no need to head out to the theater
here are a few Netflix originals you've probably

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.900
missed so far.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.880
Proving that 2019 is the year Netflix goes
totally international, Justice tells the story

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:23.269
of Farah, a young woman from the United Arab
Emirates who studied law in the United States,

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:26.580
and returns to her home city of Abu Dhabi
in order to practice.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.320
Her father is one of the top attorneys in
the UAE, and he's pleased to see Farah follow

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:36.590
in his footsteps, but there's a catch Farah
wants to work for herself and open her own

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.100
practice, but her father wants her to work
at his firm.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.780
In order to prove herself, Farah begins taking
on intriguing pro bono cases, which are based

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.180
on real cases that have gone through Abu Dhabi's
justice system.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.240
With true-to-life characters who are caught
between tradition and modernity, Justice gives

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:58.520
viewers a peek into family life in the UAE,
and the series is as educational as it is

00:00:58.520 --> 00:00:59.020
entertaining.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.180
Fatima Al Taei's portrayal of Farah is sympathetic
and relatable, and she makes the character's

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.680
ambitious nature shine through in every scene.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.440
When a series kicks off with a theme song
written by the legendary Leonard Cohen, expectations

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:17.570
are going to be high, and from the intro sequence
to the end credits, Black Earth Rising does

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:18.440
not disappoint.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.180
Protagonist Kate Ashby is rescued from the
aftermath of the Rwandan genocide as a child

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.880
by her adoptive mother, Eve, who works as
a successful international human rights lawyer.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.720
Kate eventually grows up to work side by side
with Eve as a legal investigator.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.600
When Eve prosecutes a militia leader who stood
up against genocide in the Democratic Republic

00:01:38.609 --> 00:01:43.780
of Congo and but now finds himself accused
of crimes against humanity, Kate and Eve have

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.009
to grapple with difficult questions surrounding
good, evil, the complexity of morality and

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:51.259
where they stand in their relationship with
each other.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.440
"I don't remember my family.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.540
Or my country.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.140
Nothing.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.680
I don’t know my own name!"

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.560
Black Earth Rising comes with some familiar
star power in the form of John Goodman as

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.140
Kate's employer, but it's not the kind of
series you can zone out on.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.500
Each episode pushes viewers to think critically
and refuses to spoon-feed answers to the issues

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.140
it presents.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.220
In the world of Black Earth Rising, nothing
is really black or white, and everything exists

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.220
in shades of gray.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:27.480
The Icelandic film And Breathe Normally premiered
at the Sundance Film Festival in January 2018

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.180
to overwhelmingly positive critical reception.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.940
Now, it's available for Netflix audiences
everywhere.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:38.240
Lara is a struggling single mother living
near Reykjavik who forms an unlikely bond

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.000
with Adja, a refugee seeking asylum who is
about to be deported.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.420
Lara is nothing if not stubborn, and she seems
like the last person to accept help from a

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:47.920
stranger.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.280
On the other hand, Adja has almost nothing
to give but somehow, she offers Lara what

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:58.260
little she can to support her, and Lara allows
herself to be vulnerable and let Adja into

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:58.920
her world.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.019
And Breathe Normally touches on several topics
that dominate today's headlines, from Lara's

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:08.739
attempts to disguise poverty as an adventure
for her son to scenes in the refugee center

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.040
where Adja lives in limbo.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.480
"Do you know how long I have to stay here?"

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.420
"No, I don’t know.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.960
It’s just a system."

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:25.040
This is not the side of Iceland that you see
in tourism ad campaigns — the cold, rocky

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:30.080
landscape is the backdrop for a nuanced look
at this seemingly utopian nation.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:34.700
Combine the exciting fight scenes of a martial
arts film with the tension of a drama series,

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.280
throw in some supernatural elements, and you've
got Wu Assassins.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.160
Kai Jin, a chef working in San Francisco's
Chinatown, learns his true identity: he's

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.460
actually the last of the Wu Assassins, a line
of warriors tasked with using their powers

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.800
to kill the Wu Warlords.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:57.240
The Warlords also possess magical abilities
connected to fire, earth, water, wood, and

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:57.740
metal.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.480
San Francisco is now under threat from the
warlords, and despite Kai's protests that

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.660
he's just a chef, he has no choice but to
step up, embrace his new role, and fight against

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:07.160
them.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.300
The high points of Wu Assassins are definitely
the tightly choreographed fight scenes this

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:17.900
is star Iko Uwais' first TV series, but his
previous work as a fight and action choreographer

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.000
on films like The Raid definitely prepared
him for this role.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.780
The show has received some criticism for lackluster
writing and pacing issues and a few rough

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:30.400
special effects, but if it's renewed for a
second season, the cast and crew has already

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.560
created an imaginative world of interesting
characters on which to build a strong sophomore

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.060
effort.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:41.000
The follow up to Medici: Masters of Florence,
Medici: The Magnificent takes place 20 years

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.650
after the events of the first season, and
introduces several new cast members, including

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:51.740
Sean Bean, of Game of Thrones fame, and Alessandra
Mastronardi, who you might've seen on Netflix's

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:52.660
own Master of None.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:58.300
Set in 15th century Florence, Medici: The
Magnificent continues to focus on the lives

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.840
of Florence's most influential family, the
Medici.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:07.900
After Piero de Medici is killed, his son Lorenzo
has to take control of their family-run bank.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.300
Nicknamed "Lorenzo the Magnificent," he decides
to change the way his family does business,

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.630
which stirs up trouble with Florence's other
powerful banking clan, the Pazzi.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.720
Now, Jacopo Pazzi is dead set on bringing
Lorenzo down.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.580
"a change to may bring a change to Florence.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:30.180
And with Piero recording roads there may be
better ways of destroying the Medici than

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.140
with a blade."

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.920
Fans will be happy to see this series return
with fresh faces and an engaging new plot.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:41.280
Medici: The Magnificent was certainly written
for maximum drama over historical accuracy,

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.160
but who wouldn't want to dive into centuries-old
conspiracy theories about Florentine high

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.260
society for a few hours?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.940
Soni has already been labeled the best Hindi
Netflix original so far, which is certainly

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:53.960
an impressive accolade.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.360
Headstrong protagonist Soni is a policewoman
in Delhi, a city where the justice system

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.540
rarely gives women the benefit of the doubt.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:06.340
Alongside her superintendent Kalpana, the
two have taken it upon themselves to investigate

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.760
violent crimes against women.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:12.980
The women balance each other out Soni is bold
and hotheaded, while Kalpana always manages

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:13.900
to remain calm.

00:06:14.229 --> 00:06:19.020
But when Soni is transferred out of their
department after facing allegations of misconduct,

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.320
their partnership takes a hit.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:25.420
Rather than veering into buddy cop tropes,
Soni is an unapologetically feminist film

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.540
with a thoughtful and honest depiction of
the issues that women in India face.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:34.460
Between their very different roles at work
and at home, Soni and Kalpana seem to live

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.800
double lives, a predicament that will be relatable
to audiences around the world.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.240
The Spanish horror film Ánimas is getting
mixed reviews, but if you happen to be staying

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:47.580
in on a dark and stormy night, it's the perfect
movie to fit the mood.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:53.400
Written and directed by Laura Alvea, the plot
of Ánimas is centered around Abraham and

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:58.200
Álex, friends who struggle to maintain their
close bond when Abraham begins dating his

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.260
new girlfriend Anchi.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:04.800
Somehow, Anchi's arrival into Abraham's life
kicks off a series of increasingly strange

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:09.780
and frightening events, from the death of
Abraham's abusive father to Álex's unsettling

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.590
and unexplainable visions.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:16.620
Ánimas falls squarely into the category of
atmospheric horror the flickering lighting

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:21.150
combined with the appropriately garish color
palette makes every scene feel a little bit

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:21.940
like a bad trip.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:26.300
There's a pervasive sense of isolation that
separates Álex and Abraham from the rest

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:30.630
of the world, and it always seems like they're
trapped, with no one coming to save them from

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.220
themselves.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.900
A series that starts off by introducing a
recently widowed protagonist who lost her

00:07:35.909 --> 00:07:40.780
husband in a car accident sounds like it would
lean heavier on tragedy than comedy, but Dead

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:44.600
to Me consistently dabbles in black humor
in its depiction of grief.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.370
"Just can't imagine what you’re going through."

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:52.580
"Well it’d be like if Jeff got hit by a
car and died suddenly and violently.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.500
Like that."

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:58.220
Christina Applegate stars as Jen, a young
widow is mourning the loss of her husband,

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:03.340
who meets Judy, played by Linda Cardellini,
at a support group, sparking an unlikely friendship.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:08.379
But Judy's unwavering support and carefree
attitude might not be the saving grace that

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.240
Jen was hoping for.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:14.750
When Jen invites Judy to live in her guesthouse,
she quickly finds out that Judy tends to leave

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.920
trouble in her wake, and her past is finally
catching up to her.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:22.840
Dead to Me could have gone for mainstream
drama, but the raw, realistic portrayal of

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:27.540
female friendship and appropriately dark quips
and one liners are what make it so binge-worthy.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:31.560
It dodges tired tropes at every turn and keeps
you hooked right through the finale.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:37.200
With acclaimed filmmaker Ava DuVernay serving
as the co-creator, writer, and director of

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.779
When They See Us, it's clear that the series
is a must-watch, and there's a good chance

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.920
that it will turn your worldview on its head
before the credits roll.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:49.340
DuVernay is known for her films exploring
racism and the history of civil rights in

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:54.930
the United States, like Selma and 13th, and
her skill at clearly illustrating how these

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:57.060
issues still affect our society today.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:02.380
She continues down that path with this series,
which is based on a 1989 case often referred

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.940
to as the "Central Park Five."

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.640
When a female jogger was attacked while out
running through Central Park, five young men

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:13.820
between the ages of 14 and 16, four black
and one Hispanic, were convicted of the crime

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.280
despite a lack of hard evidence.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.720
All of them served prison time, but in 2002,
their convictions were finally overturned

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.260
when DNA evidence confirmed the validity of
another man's confession.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:29.620
DuVernay actually refused to use the "Central
Park Five" moniker in the series, stating

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:31.800
she wanted the men to be seen as individuals.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:36.500
This dramatic exposé of the criminal justice
system is impossible to look away from.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.260
Hindi-language films and series are having
a moment on Netflix, proving that there's

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.940
more to India's film industry than Bollywood
musicals.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:49.560
The series Typewriter is set in Goa, a region
of India known by travelers for its popular

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:54.520
beaches and quaint fishing villages but when
three aspiring young ghost hunters decide

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:59.080
to explore a supposedly haunted villa, they
have to confront the dark forces at work in

00:09:59.080 --> 00:09:59.580
their neighborhood.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:04.040
When a new family moves into the villa, the
terrifying legends whispered about the house

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:04.660
come to life.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:10.110
Curiously enough, the haunting itself seems
to be connected to an old typewriter and trying

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.820
to remove it from the house proves to be a
dangerous mistake.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:17.790
The young protagonists setting out to solve
a supernatural mystery welcomes comparisons

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:22.680
to Stranger Things, but Typewriter isn't just
filler to hold you over until Netflix takes

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.560
you back to Hawkins.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.700
The series stands on its own, and it's legitimately
frightening.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:32.780
The overarching plot isn't particularly unique
in the horror genre, but it's undeniably binge-worthy.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:37.340
With only five episodes, you might be tempted
to watch it all in one night.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.780
Be warned: you'll probably want to sleep with
the lights on.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:45.620
They say that a dog is a man's best friend,
and the Spanish comedic drama Seventeen proves

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.740
that there's no bond like the one between
a boy and his pup.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:53.040
Hector, a troubled teen who couldn't keep
himself from getting dragged in front of a

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:57.310
judge, has spent the past two years living
in a youth detention center, and he's dedicated

00:10:57.310 --> 00:11:00.020
most of that time to trying to figure out
how to escape.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:05.160
After training a therapy dog, Sheep, as part
of a program with the local shelter, he finally

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.840
begins feeling content but when Sheep is adopted
by a new owner, Hector decides he's had enough.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:15.340
Hector breaks out of the center and gets in
touch with his brother and grandmother, enlisting

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.840
their help to track down Sheep.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.680
Sure, they'll have to commit a few crimes
and misdemeanors along the way, which has

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.280
never bothered Hector in the past.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:27.340
Now, though, there's only one catch he has
two days before he turns 18 and can be tried

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:28.180
as an adult.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:34.240
In 1988, police officer Thomas Lockhart's
obsession with tracking down an elusive serial

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.160
killer takes hold.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:39.860
Several victims in Philadelphia have bled
to death from similar wounds, and Lockhart

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:43.960
becomes convinced that if he can just crack
this difficult case, he'll finally get to

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.020
become a detective.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:49.940
But the mysterious suspect continues to thwart
him for years on end, leaving him with nothing

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:52.300
but inexplicable clues and dead ends.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:57.100
Nine years later, Lockhart has moved forward
in his career and become a detective.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:02.160
A copycat killer strikes, and as Lockhart
tries to connect the dots, he realizes that

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.080
the details just aren't adding up.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:08.140
This is not just a serial killer at work there's
something bigger at play here.

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:14.260
When Lockhart encounters his prime suspect
from 1988 and sees that she hasn't aged a

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:18.710
day, he dedicates his life to figuring out
her identity, her motives, and whether or

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.300
not she's from an entirely different time
and place.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.100
"The more I tell the more the more you’ll
keep coming after me.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.680
And I’ve seen how that turns out for you."

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:31.430
In the Shadow of the Moon is a refreshing
take on the typical police procedural, and

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:35.540
the supernatural elements keep it from feeling
like a carbon copy of similar narratives in

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.040
the genre.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:40.700
The surprising conclusion explores complex
moral issues and examines the true meaning

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:41.440
of justice.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:46.780
If you're a huge Marvel fan and you just can't
get enough of seeing superhero stories come

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:52.230
to life on screen, the charming and occasionally
nail-biting series Raising Dion might be right

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:52.900
up your alley.

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:57.940
Most popular superhero films follow well-known
comic book characters in their adult years,

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:01.420
but what were these larger-than-life figures
like as children?

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.880
"Okay can we not set anything on fire?"

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:16.200
In Raising Dion, widowed single mother Nicole
is taking care of her son Dion on her own

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.480
after the death of her husband.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:22.180
And as if the overwhelming responsibilities
of being a single mother weren't enough, Dion

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:26.260
begins exhibiting magical abilities he doesn't
quite understand it, but he's a superhero

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:26.960
in the making.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.700
Unfortunately, it's not all fun and games
for Dion.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:34.740
Powerful forces are out to exploit him for
their own ambitions, and now, Nicole must

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:35.980
enlist help to protect him.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:40.260
Plus, she needs to figure out how he developed
his powers in the first place and what his

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.140
future might hold.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.900
Beats is the latest feature offering from
director Chris Robinson, who made his feature

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:49.080
film debut with the drama ATL in 2005.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:54.370
Robinson is best known for his work directing
music videos for artists like Alicia Keys,

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:59.000
Eminem, and Nicki Minaj, and his knowledge
of the business clearly informs the plot of

00:13:59.000 --> 00:13:59.500
Beats.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:03.760
Bonus: the soundtrack is packed with songs
by up-and-coming hip hop artists.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:08.100
August is an introverted teenager who is reeling
after the loss of his sister.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:13.040
While he shuts himself away in his room and
shirks his responsibilities, he throws himself

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.440
into his only creative outlet: music.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:20.450
When school security guard Romelo drops by
his house to speak to August's mother about

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:25.399
his absence, he overhears the beats August
has been working on and is immediately intrigued

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.700
by his surprising talent.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:32.220
"Ro" has a surprise of his own up his sleeve:
he's also a music manager, and now, he wants

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.740
to take August under his wing.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:38.100
But August's heavy grief and insecurities
threaten to weigh him down as he tries to

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.140
rise to the occasion.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:40.180
"You get that?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.120
I’m not good.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:46.700
Everywhere I go I see it."

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:52.480
The story of a young underdog trying to break
into a tough industry with guidance from an

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:57.690
unexpected mentor isn't a particularly original
concept in itself, but the characters in Beats

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:58.540
are the real highlight.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:03.600
August is sensitive and conflicted, eager
to strive for more yet fragile in the wake

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:04.220
of his sister's death.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:09.480
Supporting characters, like August's protective
mother Carla, played by Orange is the New

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.440
Black's Uzo Aduba, round out a solid cast.

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:17.380
From the very first episode of The Chosen
One, you know that the outlook isn't promising

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:18.240
for the main characters.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.940
After all, messing with villagers who would
rather be left alone has been the downfall

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:25.260
of protagonists throughout film history.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:30.660
A group of doctors is sent deep into the Brazilian
wetlands to vaccinate the residents of an

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:36.440
isolated village against Zika virus, but despite
the good intentions of Lucia, Damiao, and

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:39.760
Enzo, it's clear that they're not going to
be welcomed with open arms.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:43.740
The villagers aren't just hostile because
they don't want to be bothered by outsiders.

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:48.930
They outright refuse to be vaccinated, insisting
that polluting their bodies with modern medicine

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:53.360
will cause them to lose the protection of
"The Chosen One," their local religious figure.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.420
The doctors must grapple with burning questions
of science and faith to dig up the secrets

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:02.389
at the heart of this village and determine
if something beyond their rational understanding

00:16:02.389 --> 00:16:03.340
is really at play.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:07.640
The acting in The Chosen One might feel a
bit more reminiscent of a soap opera than

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.700
prestige TV, but that doesn't detract much
from the entertainment value.

00:16:11.769 --> 00:16:16.340
And with only six addictive episodes in its
first season, it's easy to race through this

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:17.340
series in a few hours.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:22.740
The Last Czars is that kind of rare show that's
both entertaining and educational.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:28.040
This visually appealing historical drama series
switches between fictional reenactments and

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:32.940
documentary-style commentary to provide further
context, which makes for an interesting format

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:34.790
reminiscent of a History Channel program.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:39.210
It might not resonate with those who would
prefer to simply lose themselves in the story,

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:43.220
but you'll appreciate the extra background
info if you're the type who often finds yourself

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:45.300
googling questions while watching period pieces.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:50.500
If your knowledge of Russian history starts
and ends with the animated film Anastasia,

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.420
The Last Czars might help fill in a few of
the gaps.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:58.980
The series follows the life of Czar Nicholas
II, his resistance to political change, the

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:02.040
ensuing revolution, and the fall of the Romanov
dynasty.

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:07.800
If you can let a few historical inaccuracies
in the background slide, the royal scandals,

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:11.720
intricate costumes, and intriguing portrayals
of the Romanov family will more than make

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:12.220
up for it.

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:16.800
The names may sound familiar, but the series
brings these historical figures to life in

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.510
a way that explores their humanity.

